# Machine-readable citation metadata.
#
# This is the counterpart to the BibTeX block in README.md, not a replacement:
# GitHub renders its "Cite this repository" button from THIS file only, and
# JOSS reviewers look for it. The prose version stays in the README.
#
# ── TWO THINGS ARE PLACEHOLDERS AND MUST BE FILLED IN BY A HUMAN ────────────
#
#   1. `doi` under `identifiers` — commented out below. Add the Zenodo or
#      JOSS-issued DOI once it exists, and update the README's `note` field in
#      the same commit so the two cannot disagree.
#   2. `authors` — a single entry, deliberately. The author list, affiliations
#      and ORCIDs are a scholarly decision, not a mechanical one. Add
#      co-authors here and in paper.md together.
#
# `preferred-citation` is intentionally ABSENT until the JOSS paper exists.
# Adding it early would make every citation point at a paper nobody can read;
# until then the software itself is the correct thing to cite.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MApper in your research, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  MApper: A unified platform for Life Cycle Assessment, Dynamic Stock
  Modelling, prospective LCA, and Absolute Environmental Sustainability
  Assessment
abstract: >-
  MApper unifies four environmental-assessment methods behind one model:
  Life Cycle Assessment, Dynamic Stock Modelling, prospective LCA via
  IAM-derived background databases, and Absolute Environmental
  Sustainability Assessment against planetary boundaries. A product's
  identity is carried through the whole pipeline, so a cohort defined in
  the stock model is traceable into its characterised impact and into its
  share of a downscaled safe operating space. The ecoinvent database and
  IAM scenario data are separately licensed and are not distributed with
  MApper.
type: software
version: 0.2.1
license: MPL-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/leofrht-jpg/MApper-Software"
url: "https://mapper.leonardoferhati.com"

authors:
  # PLACEHOLDER — one entry. Add co-authors, affiliations and ORCIDs here and
  # in paper.md together, so the two lists cannot drift apart.
  - family-names: Ferhati
    given-names: Leonardo
    affiliation: Technical University of Denmark
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO: add

keywords:
  - life cycle assessment
  - dynamic stock modelling
  - prospective LCA
  - absolute environmental sustainability assessment
  - planetary boundaries
  - industrial ecology
  - brightway2

# identifiers:
#   # TODO: uncomment and fill once the DOI is issued. Update the README's
#   # BibTeX `note` field in the SAME commit.
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#     description: Archived software release
